<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT--Seagate cut to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT--Seagate cut to hold.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hambrecht &amp; Quist on Wednesday cut its rating on Seagate Technology to hold from buy after the disk drive maker warned of weaker earnings late Tuesday.</p>
<p>--cut fourth quarter earnings estimates to $0.65 from $0.94 and fiscal year 1998 estimate to $4.00 from $4.50.</p>
<p>--said Seagate shares are significantly undervalued at current levels but expect current problems will persist until the second quarter of 1998, keeping the stock's price under pressure until that time.</p>
</text>
